######################### SiB4 Fire Notes ################################

Because the fire emissions are provided only for the gridcell,
SiB4 handles determining the PFTs and pools that are burned
following the procedure in the technical document.

For the fire output variables, please note:
-- firec = the total carbon emitted by the fire,
           is included in the gridcell output (.g. files),
           and matches the fire emissions input from GFED.

-- fireco2 = the total CO2 emitted by the fire,
             (i.e. does not include emissions of other constituents
                   such as black carbon),
             is included in the gridcell output (.g. files),
             and matches the fire CO2 emissions input from GFED.

-- resp_fire = the fire carbon emissions per PFT,
               is included in the pft output (.pft. files) and
               is ALREADY area-weighted (unlike other variables)
                   -> the total across PFTs is the sum of contributions
                      (do not multiply by the PFT fractional coverage)
                   -> the sum of PFTs matches the fire C emissions
                      (since the fire consumed all of the carbon,
                       all carbon has been consumed from the pools
                       and included in this flux).

PLEASE NOTE:
-- If you want to include only the CO2 emissions,
you need to use the fireco2 variable.
-- Using the firec or sum of resp_fire will provide the total flux
of carbon emitted from the fire (including all constituents such as
black carbon and CO).


